      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFor a tool parameter with JSON Schema `type: \"number\"`, Qwen3 Coder converts an integer literal through `float` before returning an integer. This silently changes values above 2^53: `9007199254740993` becomes `9007199254740992`. The same path serves `step3p5` and `nanbeige`, including streaming responses, so large IDs and nanosecond timestamps can reach tools with the wrong value.\n\n## Modifications\n\nTry exact integer conversion before the existing float conversion for literals without a decimal point or exponent. Keep the existing float fallback and decimal/exponent behavior.\n\nAdd CPU tests through `FunctionCallParser` for all three aliases, unary and chunked streaming, large positive/negative integers, a nanosecond timestamp, nullable number schemas, and ordinary numeric/string/integer controls.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- New regressions: 72 failing subcases on the original code; all 4 test methods and 156 subcases pass after the fix.\n- Existing Qwen3 Coder tests plus new tests: 21 passed.\n- Broader existing parser module: 235 passed; 15 DeepSeek V3.2/V4 tests cannot initialize their tokenizer fixtures on this CPU-only environment because `triton` is unavailable.\n- Touched-file pre-commit checks passed, including CPU CI registration.\n\nLocal tests load the actual parser, protocol and test modules while excluding SGLang's GPU-facing package initializers. No parser implementation is replaced. No GPU/model-output benchmark was run.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo inference performance claim; this changes numeric argument fidelity.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format code with pre-commit.\n- [x] Add registered CPU tests and before/after reproduction.\n- [x] Follow the existing parser style.\n- [x] No user-facing documentation change is needed for this correctness fix.\n\nDeveloped with AI assistance. Root and an independent agent reviewed the change; the focused test suite was also rerun independently.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #36852108386](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36852108386)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #36852108111](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36852108111)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #36852108740](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/36852108740)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
